{"id":"aholibamah","name":"Aholibamah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:aholibamah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Aholibamah","text":"Tent of the height, the name given to Judith, the daughter of Beeri = Anah (Gen. 26:34; 36:2), when she became the wife of Esau. A district among the mountains of Edom, probably near Mount Hor, was called after her name, or it may be that she received her name from the district. From her descended three tribes of Edomites, founded by her three sons."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H173","lemma":"אׇהֳלִיבָמָה","xlit":"ʼOhŏlîybâmâh","gloss":"Oholibamah, a wife of Esau","kjv":"Aholibamah","count":3,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","xlit":"bath","gloss":"a daughter","kjv":"apple, branch, company, daughter","count":4,"share":0.8},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":3,"share":0.6}],"verses":["Gen.36.14","Gen.36.25","Gen.36.41","Gen.26.34","Gen.36.3"],"related":[{"id":"ajah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"},{"id":"anah","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"},{"id":"asenath","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"},{"id":"beth-shean","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"},{"id":"daughter","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"},{"id":"daughter-in-law","type":"lexical","strong":"H1323","why":"both lead with בַּת (H1323)"}],"works":[{"work":"antiquities","title":"Antiquities of the Jews","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"AntI.18","count":1,"book":"Ant. 1","title":"Concerning The Sons Of Isaac, Esau And Jacob; Of Their Nativity And Education."}]}]}
